      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"UXM266\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/48/1966_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> UXM266:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm having an issue where it's not responsive when trying to select decks. I can't scroll the Villains, and it added an hero that I didn't choose.<br>It seems very, very slow…<br>I too blame apple</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yeah. On both me and my wife's iPad, it's very sluggish when choosing decks for a new game. It's difficult … And sometimes near impossible … to scroll through all the decks. And then sometimes a hero or villain will pop in when all you're trying to do is scroll past them. Turning off decks, so there's less to choose from, helps a lot … though limiting.</p>",
